'''EVOS Divine''' (formerly '''EVOS Capital''' or '''EVOS Esports ID''') is an Indonesian Free Fire team under '''EVOS Esports''', a Southeast Asia gaming multi-organization based in [[:category:Indonesia|Indonesia]].

==History==
'''EVOS Esports''' was founded and is operated by '''Ivan "ToxiCEO" Yeo''', '''Wesley Yiu''', '''Michael "Mike" Wijaya''', and '''Hartman Harris'''. The organization was established in '''2016''' as a newly formed '''[https://liquipedia.net/dota2/EVOS_Esports Dota 2]''' team. Over time, EVOS achieved numerous title wins and successful title defenses, quickly earning widespread recognition and respect in the esports scene. As the organization evolved, its '''Dota 2''' and '''Point Blank''' divisions were disbanded, making way for new teams in titles such as '''Mobile Legends''', '''Free Fire''', and '''PUBG Mobile'''.

In April 2019, EVOS entered the Free Fire competitive scene by acquiring the roster of '''Capital Esports''', rebranding the team as '''EVOS Capital'''. This year also marked a golden year for [https://www.evos.gg/ EVOS Esports], as the organization secured global titles in two major esports disciplines. The Free Fire division won the [[Free_Fire_World_Cup/2019|Free Fire World Cup 2019]] in {{FlagNoLink|th}} Bangkok, while the Mobile Legends division claimed victory at the [[mobilelegends:M1_World_Championship|M1 World Championship 2019]] in {{FlagNoLink|my}} Kuala Lumpur. By December 2019, the team officially changed its name to '''EVOS Esports''' (or '''EVOS Esports ID''' to distinguish from [[EVOS Phoenix|Thai lineup]]).

Since mid-2021, the team is known as '''EVOS Divine''' has been used until now and Thai lineup has been called '''[[EVOS Phoenix]]'''.

As of 2025, EVOS has secured a total of four world championship titles in Free Fire, solidifying its status as one of the most successful organizations in the game’s history:

*'''EVOS Capital''' (now known as {{Team|evos id}}) won the [[Free_Fire_World_Cup/2019|Free Fire World Cup 2019]] in {{FlagNoLink|th}} Bangkok.

*Due to tournament rules, {{Team|evos th}} competed under the name {{Team|evos phoenix as force}} and won the [[Free_Fire_World_Series/2021/Singapore|Free Fire World Series 2021]] in {{FlagNoLink|sg}} Singapore.

*{{Team|evos th}} continued their reign by winning the [[Free_Fire_World_Series/2022/Bangkok|Free Fire World Series 2022]], in {{FlagNoLink|th}} Bangkok.

*{{Team|evos id}} reclaimed the world title at the [[Esports_World_Cup/2025|Esports World Cup 2025]] in {{FlagNoLink|sa}} Riyadh.

These achievements underscore EVOS’s legacy as a dominant and consistent force in the international Free Fire competitive scene, particularly through its Indonesian and Thai divisions.

